  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Dicastery for Promoting Integral Human Development &amp; Caritas Internationalis  COVID-19 Response Fund</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">To meet the challenges posed by the COVID-19 pandemic, the Dicastery for Promoting Integral Human Development and Caritas Internationalis are establishing a COVID-19 Response Fund (CRF).

The fund will prioritise the provision of health care related services by Catholic organizations and Caritas. It will focus on: 
&#x2022; Infection prevention and control (IPC) 
&#x2022; Community case management 
&#x2022; Water and Sanitation and Hygiene Promotion (WASH) in healthcare SETTINGS 
&#x2022; Procurement of Personal Protective Equipment (PPE) and other supplies 

The CRF will also consider proposals that aim to mitigate the impact of COVID-19 by: 
&#x2022; working with communities on Risk Communication and Community Engagement for behavioural change; 
&#x2022; reinforcing community services, including ensuring food security of the most vulnerable through in-kind or cash-based programming, child protection, psycho-social assistance</narrative>
  </description>
